s it:\n- Develops a piece with tempo toward f7\n- Supports potential tactics\n- Is a natural Italian Game setup\n\nBetween these two, the bishop development is more urgent since I need to complete kingside development and prepare castling.\n\nReason: Developing the light-squared bishop to c4 is the most natural continuation. It develops a piece, targets the weak f7 square, prepares kingside castling, and maintains the initiative. This follows classical opening principles of rapid development while keeping pressure on Black's position.\n\nAnswer: B: f1-c4"}
